// =============================================================================
// Engrisk — PostgreSQL domain model (design artifact, not a migration)
// Companion docs: apps/ux_preview/product_flow.md (section J maps UX → tables)
// Validated with @dbml/cli dbml2sql --postgres and applied to PostgreSQL 14.
// =============================================================================

Project engrisk {
  database_type: 'PostgreSQL'
  Note: '''
# Engrisk data model

**Scope.** TOEIC + IELTS practice, mock exams, review, AI tutor/evaluation, learner uploads.
Phase 1 runs as ONE logical product (the platform tenant). The model is multi-tenant-ready.

## Domains (TableGroups)
1. identity_access   — global users, auth identities, sessions, RBAC
2. tenancy           — tenants, memberships, entitlements, invitations
3. assets_uploads    — files in object storage + learner source materials
4. exam_content      — exam types, skills, question bank, exams, immutable revisions
5. learning_records  — goals, attempts, responses, evaluations, scores, skill stats
6. ai                — AI run provenance + AI tutor conversations

## Tenant isolation strategy
- **Global (no tenant_id):** users, auth_*, permissions, system roles, exam_types, skills.
- **Tenant-owned roots carry NOT NULL tenant_id:** content, exams, attempts, goals, AI runs.
- **Children inherit** tenant via parent (responses → attempts, messages → conversations),
  except where tenant_id is needed to enforce a composite FK (exam_revisions, exam_revision_items).
- **Composite FKs** `(tenant_id, x_id) → parent(tenant_id, id)` make cross-tenant links
  impossible inside authoring graphs (question → group, revision item → question, ...).
- **Learner data → membership:** `(tenant_id, user_id) → tenant_memberships(tenant_id, user_id)`
  guarantees learner records only exist inside a tenant the user belongs to.
- **Single intentional cross-tenant edge:** learner records may reference PUBLISHED content
  owned by the platform tenant (visibility = public) or licensed via exam_licenses.
  Content never references learner data.
- **Phase 1** isolation = service layer always scopes by the session's active tenant.
- **Future RLS:** `SET LOCAL app.tenant_id / app.user_id` per transaction; policy on each
  tenant-owned root: `tenant_id = current_setting('app.tenant_id')::uuid` plus a read policy
  for published public/licensed content. Child tables get `EXISTS (parent)` policies
  (or a denormalized tenant_id if profiling demands). No RLS migration is generated now.

## Default platform tenant
A seeded tenant (kind = platform, slug = 'engrisk') owns global content and all B2C
learners' memberships. This avoids `tenant_id IS NULL` meaning "global" (which breaks
uniqueness, composite FKs and RLS) and means B2B later is "add tenants", not "add tenant_id".

## Content reuse & versioning (copy-on-write)
- question_groups / questions are **immutable once published**. Editing a published row
  creates a new row (version + 1, same lineage_id, supersedes_id → old) and marks the old
  row 'superseded'. Old exam revisions keep pointing at the old row.
- exams are stable catalog products; exam_revisions are **immutable published snapshots**
  that list exact question versions (exam_revision_items).
- attempts pin an exam_revision; responses pin an exact question version. Historical
  results therefore never change when content is edited.
- AI-generated questions use the SAME tables (origin = ai_generated + ai_run_id provenance).

## Sensitive data
- answer_key, rubric_key, explanation, transcript are server-only until the attempt
  permits review (practice: after answering; mock: after submit). Enforce in API DTOs;
  optionally with PostgreSQL column-level GRANTs for a read-only delivery role.
- Only password HASHES (argon2id) and token HASHES are stored. OAuth tokens are not stored.
- Binary files live in object storage; PostgreSQL stores storage keys + metadata only.

## Conventions
- uuid PKs (`gen_random_uuid()`, PG13+). snake_case, plural tables, `<entity>_id` FKs.
- timestamptz everywhere. `citext` for emails (extension `citext`).
- DBML enums document allowed values; implement as `text + CHECK` (cheaper to evolve)
  unless the set is truly frozen.
- Partial unique indexes are documented in index notes (DBML cannot express WHERE).
- JSONB only for (a) type-specific question payloads validated by Pydantic schemas,
  (b) immutable snapshots, (c) small config blobs. Never for relational facts.

## Phase tags
Every table note starts with [P1] … [P4] = roadmap phase in which the table is first needed.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// ENUMS (documented value sets — see Conventions)
// =============================================================================

Enum user_kind {
  guest [note: 'Anonymous learner created on first practice; no auth identity yet']
  registered
}

Enum user_status {
  active
  suspended
  deleted [note: 'Soft-deleted + PII scrubbed; row kept for referential history']
}

Enum auth_provider {
  password
  google
  apple [note: 'Future']
  microsoft [note: 'Future']
  oidc [note: 'Future enterprise SSO per tenant']
}

Enum auth_token_purpose {
  email_verification
  password_reset
}

Enum tenant_kind {
  platform [note: 'Exactly one: Engrisk itself. Owns global content and B2C memberships']
  organization [note: 'Phase 4: language centers, schools, companies']
}

Enum tenant_status {
  active
  suspended
  archived
}

Enum membership_status {
  active
  suspended
  left
}

Enum role_scope {
  platform [note: 'Granted via platform_role_assignments; cross-tenant powers']
  tenant [note: 'Granted via membership_roles; powers inside one tenant']
}

Enum asset_kind {
  audio
  image
  document
}

Enum asset_purpose {
  question_media [note: 'Listening audio, charts, photos used by question_groups']
  source_material [note: 'Learner/teacher upload used for AI generation']
  learner_response [note: 'Speaking recordings']
  branding [note: 'Tenant logos']
}

Enum asset_status {
  pending_upload
  available
  quarantined [note: 'Failed malware/content scan']
  deleted
}

Enum rights_basis {
  own_work
  licensed
  public_domain
  personal_study_only [note: 'May never be published beyond the owner']
}

Enum material_status {
  uploaded
  processing
  ready
  failed
  rejected [note: 'Policy/safety rejection']
}

Enum skill_area {
  listening
  reading
  writing
  speaking
}

Enum content_status {
  draft
  in_review
  published [note: 'Immutable from here on']
  superseded [note: 'A newer version exists; still valid for old revisions']
  archived [note: 'Not selectable for new exams']
}

Enum content_visibility {
  private [note: 'Owner only (owner_user_id)']
  tenant [note: 'Members of the owning tenant']
  public [note: 'Platform tenant only: whole platform catalog']
}

Enum content_origin {
  human
  ai_generated
  imported
}

Enum question_type {
  single_choice
  multiple_choice
  fill_blank
  matching
  ordering
  short_answer
  essay [note: 'IELTS Writing; evaluated, not key-graded']
  speaking [note: 'IELTS Speaking; audio answer, evaluated']
}

Enum stimulus_type {
  passage
  audio
  image
  audio_image
}

Enum exam_kind {
  full_mock [note: 'Full timed test, always mock mode']
  section_test [note: 'One section, e.g. TOEIC Reading Part 7']
  practice_set [note: 'Short curated set, 5–15 min']
  personal_practice [note: 'Built by a learner from own approved generated questions']
}

Enum exam_status {
  draft
  published
  archived
}

Enum revision_status {
  draft
  published [note: 'Immutable']
  retired [note: 'No new attempts; history intact']
}

Enum access_tier {
  guest [note: 'Playable without an account']
  registered
  premium [note: 'Requires entitlement (future monetization)']
}

Enum attempt_mode {
  practice [note: 'Instant feedback allowed, pausable, listening replay allowed']
  mock [note: 'Exam rules: server deadline, no feedback until submit, single audio play']
}

Enum attempt_status {
  in_progress
  submitted [note: 'Objective grading done; subjective evaluations pending']
  completed [note: 'All scores final for this attempt']
  abandoned
}

Enum submit_reason {
  learner
  time_expired
}

Enum evaluator_kind {
  ai
  human
}

Enum evaluation_status {
  pending
  completed
  failed
  superseded
}

Enum score_kind {
  raw [note: 'Points earned / max points. Deterministic']
  scaled_estimate [note: 'Exam scale via unofficial conversion table (TOEIC 10–990, IELTS band)']
  ai_estimate [note: 'AI-evaluated band for Writing/Speaking. Never official']
}

Enum goal_status {
  active
  achieved
  archived
}

Enum ai_purpose {
  explanation
  tutor_reply
  writing_evaluation
  speaking_evaluation
  transcription
  question_generation
}

Enum ai_run_status {
  queued
  running
  succeeded
  failed
  cancelled
}

Enum message_sender {
  learner
  tutor
  system
}

// =============================================================================
// 1. IDENTITY & ACCESS (global)
// =============================================================================

Table users {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  kind user_kind [not null, default: 'registered']
  status user_status [not null, default: 'active']
  email citext [note: 'Primary contact/login email. NULL for guests. Unique when not null']
  email_verified_at timestamptz
  display_name text
  avatar_url text [note: 'External URL (e.g. Google picture) or signed URL; no binary']
  locale text [not null, default: 'vi-VN']
  timezone text [not null, default: 'Asia/Ho_Chi_Minh']
  preferences jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"study_reminder":{"enabled":true,"time":"20:00"}} — small personal settings read as a whole']
  registered_at timestamptz [note: 'Set when a guest converts or a user signs up']
  last_seen_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    email [unique, name: 'uq_users_email', note: 'Partial: WHERE email IS NOT NULL']
    (kind, created_at) [name: 'ix_users_guest_cleanup', note: 'Partial: WHERE kind = guest — expire unconverted guests']
  }

  checks {
    `kind = 'guest' OR email IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_users_registered_has_email']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Global person identity. Holds NO credentials, NO roles, NO tenant data.
Guest → account conversion keeps the same users.id (kind guest → registered + new
auth_identity), so attempts made as a guest need no data migration.
'''
}

Table auth_identities {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]
  provider auth_provider [not null]
  provider_subject text [not null, note: 'Google "sub"; for password = normalized email']
  provider_email citext [note: 'Email asserted by the provider at last login']
  password_hash text [note: 'argon2id hash. Only for provider = password']
  last_used_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (provider, provider_subject) [unique, name: 'uq_auth_identities_provider_subject']
    (user_id, provider) [unique, name: 'uq_auth_identities_user_provider', note: 'One identity per provider per user']
  }

  checks {
    `(provider = 'password') = (password_hash IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_auth_identities_password_hash']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] How a user proves who they are. N identities → 1 user (email+password, Google, future
Apple/Microsoft/tenant OIDC). Adding a provider = new enum value + adapter; users unchanged.
Account linking: a verified Google email matching users.email links after re-auth.
'''
}

Table auth_sessions {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]
  active_tenant_id uuid [not null, note: 'Tenant context for this session; switching tenants updates this']
  refresh_token_hash bytea [not null, note: 'SHA-256 of opaque rotating refresh token']
  user_agent text
  ip_address inet
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  last_used_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]
  revoked_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    refresh_token_hash [unique, name: 'uq_auth_sessions_refresh_token_hash']
    user_id [name: 'ix_auth_sessions_user']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Refresh-token session (access tokens are short-lived JWTs carrying user_id +
active_tenant_id). Composite FK to tenant_memberships ensures the active tenant is one the
user belongs to. Tenant switch = membership check + update active_tenant_id + new access token.
'''
}

Table auth_tokens {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]
  purpose auth_token_purpose [not null]
  token_hash bytea [not null]
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]
  consumed_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    token_hash [unique, name: 'uq_auth_tokens_token_hash']
    (user_id, purpose) [name: 'ix_auth_tokens_user_purpose']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Single-use email verification and password reset tokens (hash only).'
}

Table roles {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [ref: > tenants.id, note: 'NULL = system role (seeded). Set = tenant custom role (P4)']
  key text [not null, note: 'learner, teacher, content_manager, tenant_admin, platform_admin, platform_support']
  name text [not null]
  scope role_scope [not null]
  description text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, key) [unique, name: 'uq_roles_tenant_key', note: 'PG15+: NULLS NOT DISTINCT; on PG14 add partial unique (key) WHERE tenant_id IS NULL']
    (id, scope) [unique, name: 'uq_roles_id_scope', note: 'Target of scope-checked composite FKs']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] RBAC role = named bundle of permissions. Roles never appear as columns on business
tables. Seeded P1: learner; content_manager (granted inside the PLATFORM tenant to the
Engrisk content team, so platform content is authored like any tenant content);
platform_admin, platform_support (platform scope). Seeded P4: teacher, tenant_admin.
Tenant-defined roles are a P4 extension (tenant_id set).
'''
}

Table permissions {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  key text [not null, unique, note: 'resource.action, e.g. exam.take, content.publish, member.manage']
  scope role_scope [not null]
  description text

  Note: '[P1] Permission catalog, seeded from code. Checked by FastAPI dependencies, never by role name.'
}

Table role_permissions {
  role_id uuid [not null, ref: > roles.id]
  permission_id uuid [not null, ref: > permissions.id]

  indexes {
    (role_id, permission_id) [pk]
  }

  Note: '[P1] Role ↔ permission. Platform-scope permissions may only attach to platform-scope roles (seed check).'
}

Table platform_role_assignments {
  user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]
  role_id uuid [not null]
  role_scope role_scope [not null, default: 'platform']
  granted_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (user_id, role_id) [pk]
  }

  checks {
    `role_scope = 'platform'` [name: 'ck_platform_role_assignments_scope']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Platform staff (platform_admin, platform_support). Kept separate from tenant
membership so B2C learner membership in the platform tenant never implies staff power.
Composite FK (role_id, role_scope) → roles(id, scope) makes assigning a tenant role here impossible.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 2. TENANCY
// =============================================================================

Table tenants {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  kind tenant_kind [not null]
  status tenant_status [not null, default: 'active']
  slug text [not null, unique, note: 'URL-safe; platform tenant = engrisk']
  name text [not null]
  branding jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{display_name, logo_asset_id, accent_color, support_email}. Read as one blob, never queried']
  default_locale text [not null, default: 'vi-VN']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    kind [name: 'uq_tenants_single_platform', note: 'Partial unique: (kind) WHERE kind = platform — exactly one platform tenant']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1 seeded / P4 self-serve] Organization boundary. Phase 1 has exactly one row (platform).
Branding lives in JSONB because it is presentation config read as a whole; the UI maps
accent_color onto the HeroUI --accent token. Custom domains (P4) → future tenant_domains table.
'''
}

Table tenant_memberships {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]
  status membership_status [not null, default: 'active']
  joined_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id) [unique, name: 'uq_tenant_memberships_tenant_user', note: 'Target of all learner-data composite FKs']
    user_id [name: 'ix_tenant_memberships_user', note: 'Tenant switcher: list my tenants']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] A user belongs to N tenants. Phase 1: signup (and guest creation) auto-creates a
membership in the platform tenant with role learner. Memberships are never hard-deleted
(status = left) so historical attempts keep a valid parent.
'''
}

Table membership_roles {
  membership_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenant_memberships.id]
  role_id uuid [not null]
  role_scope role_scope [not null, default: 'tenant']
  granted_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (membership_id, role_id) [pk]
  }

  checks {
    `role_scope = 'tenant'` [name: 'ck_membership_roles_scope']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Tenant-scoped role grants (a teacher can also be content_manager). Composite FK
(role_id, role_scope) → roles(id, scope) blocks granting platform roles via membership.
App rule: a custom role (roles.tenant_id set) must belong to the membership's tenant.
'''
}

Table tenant_entitlements {
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  feature_key text [not null, note: 'ai_tutor, writing_ai_feedback, speaking_ai_feedback, material_upload, question_generation, platform_library, custom_branding']
  is_enabled boolean [not null, default: true]
  limits jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'e.g. {"ai_requests_per_user_per_day": 30}']
  source text [not null, default: 'plan', note: 'plan | override | trial']
  valid_until timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, feature_key) [pk]
  }

  Note: '''
[P1 seeded for platform tenant] Effective feature switches per tenant. Plans/billing live in
code/config until monetization (future: plans + subscriptions tables, incl. B2C user-level
premium). Feature checks read entitlements, never plan names.
'''
}

Table tenant_invitations {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  email citext [not null]
  role_id uuid [not null, ref: > roles.id]
  token_hash bytea [not null]
  invited_by_user_id uuid [not null, ref: > users.id]
  expires_at timestamptz [not null]
  accepted_at timestamptz
  accepted_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  revoked_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    token_hash [unique, name: 'uq_tenant_invitations_token_hash']
    (tenant_id, email) [name: 'ix_tenant_invitations_tenant_email']
  }

  Note: '[P4] Join-organization flow. Acceptance creates tenant_memberships + membership_roles. Role must be tenant-scope (checked at acceptance).'
}

// =============================================================================
// 3. CONTENT ASSETS & LEARNER UPLOADS
// =============================================================================

Table content_assets {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  owner_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id, note: 'Uploader; NULL for system-imported media']
  kind asset_kind [not null]
  purpose asset_purpose [not null]
  status asset_status [not null, default: 'pending_upload']
  storage_key text [not null, note: 'Object storage key (S3/GCS compatible). Served via short-lived signed URLs after authz']
  mime_type text [not null]
  byte_size bigint
  sha256 bytea [note: 'Dedup + integrity']
  duration_ms integer [note: 'Audio only']
  metadata jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'width/height, page_count, scan result']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  deleted_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    storage_key [unique, name: 'uq_content_assets_storage_key']
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_content_assets_tenant_id', note: 'Composite FK target']
    (tenant_id, owner_user_id, purpose) [name: 'ix_content_assets_owner']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Every binary file (listening audio, images, PDFs, speaking recordings, logos).
Access is decided by the referencing entity (question_group, source_material, response),
never by the asset alone. Upload flow: create row (pending_upload) → presigned PUT →
scan → available | quarantined.
'''
}

Table source_materials {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  owner_user_id uuid [not null]
  asset_id uuid [not null]
  title text [not null]
  rights_basis rights_basis [not null]
  rights_confirmed_at timestamptz [not null, note: 'Learner confirmed they may use this material']
  status material_status [not null, default: 'uploaded']
  failure_reason text
  extracted_text text [note: 'Text extracted for generation (TOAST-compressed). Never shown to other users']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  deleted_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_source_materials_tenant_id']
    (tenant_id, owner_user_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_source_materials_owner']
  }

  Note: '''
[P3] A learning document uploaded to generate practice. Always private to its owner.
Lifecycle: uploaded → processing → ready | failed | rejected. Questions generated from it
start as private drafts; it NEVER feeds the public bank automatically. Material with
rights_basis = personal_study_only can never back tenant/public content (service rule).
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 4. EXAM CONTENT (question bank + exams)
// =============================================================================

Table exam_types {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  code text [not null, unique, note: 'toeic_lr, ielts_academic, ielts_general; later toeic_sw, cambridge_*']
  name text [not null]
  scoring_policy_key text [not null, note: 'Code-defined scorer, e.g. toeic_lr_v1, ielts_v1']
  score_scale jsonb [not null, note: 'UI bounds for goals: {"min":10,"max":990,"step":5} or {"min":0,"max":9,"step":0.5}']
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]

  Note: '''
[P1] Global catalog of exam formats. A new format = new row + scorer + section layout in
exam_revisions.sections — no new tables. Tenant-defined exam types are not supported yet.
'''
}

Table skills {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  code text [not null, unique, note: 'e.g. reading.inference, grammar.verb_tense, toeic.part2.question_response']
  name text [not null]
  area skill_area [not null]
  exam_type_id uuid [ref: > exam_types.id, note: 'NULL = cross-exam skill (grammar, vocabulary, inference)']
  parent_id uuid [ref: > skills.id]
  position smallint [not null, default: 0]
  is_active boolean [not null, default: true]

  indexes {
    (area, exam_type_id) [name: 'ix_skills_area_exam_type']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Global skill taxonomy (2 levels in practice). Replaces a separate tags system:
everything we analyse ("weak skills") is a skill. Free-form topics are not modeled.
'''
}

Table question_groups {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  lineage_id uuid [not null, note: 'Stable identity across versions (= id of version 1)']
  version integer [not null, default: 1]
  supersedes_id uuid [ref: > question_groups.id]
  exam_type_id uuid [ref: > exam_types.id]
  stimulus_type stimulus_type [not null]
  title text
  content jsonb [not null, note: 'Passage rich text / instructions. Schema per stimulus_type']
  audio_asset_id uuid
  image_asset_id uuid
  transcript text [note: 'PROTECTED: listening transcript, revealed only in review']
  status content_status [not null, default: 'draft']
  visibility content_visibility [not null, default: 'tenant']
  owner_user_id uuid [note: 'Required when visibility = private']
  origin content_origin [not null, default: 'human']
  ai_run_id uuid [ref: > ai_runs.id]
  source_material_id uuid
  created_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  published_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_question_groups_tenant_id']
    (lineage_id, version) [unique, name: 'uq_question_groups_lineage_version']
    (tenant_id, status, exam_type_id) [name: 'ix_question_groups_bank']
  }

  checks {
    `visibility <> 'private' OR owner_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_question_groups_private_owner']
    `origin <> 'ai_generated' OR ai_run_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_question_groups_ai_provenance']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Shared stimulus for several questions: a reading passage (TOEIC Part 6/7, IELTS
passage), a conversation audio (TOEIC Part 3/4), a chart (IELTS Writing Task 1).
Standalone questions (TOEIC Part 2/5) have no group. Copy-on-write versioning: revising a
published group clones the group AND its questions into a new version.
'''
}

Table questions {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  lineage_id uuid [not null, note: 'Stable identity across versions; analytics aggregate by lineage']
  version integer [not null, default: 1]
  supersedes_id uuid [ref: > questions.id]
  question_group_id uuid
  group_position smallint [note: 'Order inside the group']
  exam_type_id uuid [ref: > exam_types.id]
  question_type question_type [not null]
  prompt jsonb [not null, note: 'Learner-visible payload: stem, options [{key,text}], blanks, word limits, speaking prep/answer seconds. Schema per question_type']
  answer_key jsonb [note: 'PROTECTED. {"choice":"B"} | {"accept":["..."]} | {"order":[...]}. NULL for essay/speaking']
  rubric_key text [note: 'For essay/speaking: versioned rubric id, e.g. ielts_writing_task2_v1']
  explanation jsonb [note: 'PROTECTED until review. Verified explanation {text, evidence_span}']
  review_flags jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'Reviewer-only quality flags from AI/validators, e.g. [{"code":"ambiguous_key","detail":"A and D plausible"}]. Never sent to learners']
  difficulty smallint [not null, default: 3]
  default_points numeric(5,2) [not null, default: 1]
  status content_status [not null, default: 'draft']
  visibility content_visibility [not null, default: 'tenant']
  owner_user_id uuid [note: 'Required when visibility = private']
  origin content_origin [not null, default: 'human']
  ai_run_id uuid [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Generation run when origin = ai_generated']
  source_material_id uuid [note: 'Upload the question was generated from']
  created_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  reviewed_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id, note: 'Human who approved for publication']
  reviewed_at timestamptz
  published_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_questions_tenant_id']
    (lineage_id, version) [unique, name: 'uq_questions_lineage_version']
    (tenant_id, status, exam_type_id, question_type) [name: 'ix_questions_bank']
    (question_group_id, group_position) [name: 'ix_questions_group']
    source_material_id [name: 'ix_questions_source_material']
  }

  checks {
    `difficulty BETWEEN 1 AND 5` [name: 'ck_questions_difficulty']
    `visibility <> 'private' OR owner_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_questions_private_owner']
    `origin <> 'ai_generated' OR ai_run_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_questions_ai_provenance']
    `question_type IN ('essay','speaking') OR answer_key IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_questions_objective_has_key']
    `question_type NOT IN ('essay','speaking') OR rubric_key IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_questions_subjective_has_rubric']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] ONE question bank for TOEIC, IELTS, human-authored, imported and AI-generated items.
All 8 question types share this table; type-specific shape lives in prompt/answer_key JSONB
(validated by Pydantic models keyed by question_type) instead of 8 sub-tables or EAV.
Lifecycle: draft → in_review → published → superseded/archived. Published rows are
immutable (enforced by service + optional trigger). AI-generated items additionally need
reviewed_by_user_id before status = published (service rule; private personal-practice
items are "reviewed" by their owner).
'''
}

Table question_skills {
  question_id uuid [not null, ref: > questions.id]
  skill_id uuid [not null, ref: > skills.id]
  is_primary boolean [not null, default: false]

  indexes {
    (question_id, skill_id) [pk]
    skill_id [name: 'ix_question_skills_skill']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Skill tagging that powers per-skill results, weak-skill detection and targeted practice. Copied with the question on new versions.'
}

Table exams {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  exam_type_id uuid [not null, ref: > exam_types.id]
  slug text [not null]
  title text [not null]
  description text
  kind exam_kind [not null]
  skill_focus skill_area [note: 'NULL = mixed / full test. Drives catalog skill filter']
  difficulty smallint [not null, default: 3, note: 'UI: 1–2 Easy, 3 Medium, 4–5 Hard']
  access_tier access_tier [not null, default: 'registered']
  status exam_status [not null, default: 'draft']
  visibility content_visibility [not null, default: 'tenant']
  owner_user_id uuid [note: 'Learner who owns a personal_practice exam']
  current_revision_id uuid [ref: - exam_revisions.id, note: 'Revision served to NEW attempts']
  created_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_exams_tenant_id']
    (tenant_id, slug) [unique, name: 'uq_exams_tenant_slug']
    (tenant_id, status, exam_type_id, kind, skill_focus) [name: 'ix_exams_catalog']
    (tenant_id, owner_user_id) [name: 'ix_exams_owner', note: 'Partial: WHERE owner_user_id IS NOT NULL']
  }

  checks {
    `difficulty BETWEEN 1 AND 5` [name: 'ck_exams_difficulty']
    `visibility <> 'private' OR owner_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_exams_private_owner']
    `kind <> 'personal_practice' OR visibility = 'private'` [name: 'ck_exams_personal_is_private']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Catalog product: "TOEIC Mini Mock 01", "IELTS Reading – Matching Headings Set 2".
"Practice set" and "full mock" are the same entity with a different kind — one attempt
engine, one catalog. Stable slug/URL; content lives in exam_revisions.
Visibility public is only allowed for the platform tenant (service rule).
'''
}

Table exam_revisions {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null]
  exam_id uuid [not null]
  revision_number integer [not null]
  status revision_status [not null, default: 'draft']
  sections jsonb [not null, note: '[{key:"L", title, skill_area, time_limit_seconds, instructions, rules:{audio_replay:false}}]']
  time_limit_seconds integer [note: 'Total limit for mock; NULL = untimed practice']
  question_count integer [not null, default: 0, note: 'Snapshot at publish (immutable) for catalog listing']
  max_points numeric(7,2) [not null, default: 0, note: 'Snapshot at publish']
  scoring_policy_key text [not null, note: 'Copied from exam_types at publish; pins the scorer version']
  published_at timestamptz
  published_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, id) [unique, name: 'uq_exam_revisions_tenant_id']
    (exam_id, revision_number) [unique, name: 'uq_exam_revisions_exam_number']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Immutable published snapshot of an exam's structure. Sections are JSONB because
they are tiny, immutable, always read with the revision and never referenced by FK
(responses store section_key). Editing a published exam = new draft revision → publish →
exams.current_revision_id moves. In-progress attempts finish on their pinned revision.
'''
}

Table exam_revision_items {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null]
  exam_revision_id uuid [not null]
  section_key text [not null, note: 'Matches exam_revisions.sections[].key (validated at publish)']
  position integer [not null, note: 'Global display order = question number']
  question_id uuid [not null, note: 'Exact question VERSION']
  points numeric(5,2) [not null, default: 1]

  indexes {
    (exam_revision_id, position) [unique, name: 'uq_exam_revision_items_position']
    (exam_revision_id, question_id) [unique, name: 'uq_exam_revision_items_question']
    question_id [name: 'ix_exam_revision_items_question', note: 'Where is this question used?']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Ordered questions in a revision. Same question version may appear in many
revisions/exams (reuse). Groups are rendered from questions.question_group_id, so a
practice set may pick a subset of a passage's questions. Composite FKs keep exam and
questions in the same tenant.
'''
}

Table exam_licenses {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  exam_id uuid [not null, ref: > exams.id]
  licensee_tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  granted_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  starts_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  ends_at timestamptz
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (exam_id, licensee_tenant_id) [unique, name: 'uq_exam_licenses_exam_tenant']
    licensee_tenant_id [name: 'ix_exam_licenses_licensee']
  }

  Note: '''
[P4] Cross-tenant sharing at EXAM granularity (not question level): licensee members can
attempt the licensed exam's current revision; content stays owned and edited by the owner.
Alternative coarse grant: tenant_entitlements.platform_library = all public platform exams.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 5. LEARNING RECORDS
// =============================================================================

Table learner_goals {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  exam_type_id uuid [not null, ref: > exam_types.id]
  status goal_status [not null, default: 'active']
  self_assessed_level text [note: 'Onboarding answer: new | basic | intermediate | advanced']
  baseline_score numeric(6,2) [note: 'Optional: previous score the learner reports (self-reported, not verified)']
  target_score numeric(6,2) [note: 'TOEIC 10–990 or IELTS band; bounds from exam_types.score_scale']
  target_date date
  weekly_study_minutes smallint
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, exam_type_id) [name: 'ix_learner_goals_user', note: 'Partial unique: WHERE status = active (one active goal per exam type)']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Onboarding output and the basis for "recommended next" + goal progress. Skipping
onboarding simply means no row; the dashboard then asks for a goal inline.
'''
}

Table attempts {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, note: 'Tenant context the learner practised in']
  user_id uuid [not null]
  exam_revision_id uuid [ref: > exam_revisions.id, note: 'Pinned revision. NULL only for system-composed adaptive practice (P2)']
  mode attempt_mode [not null]
  status attempt_status [not null, default: 'in_progress']
  settings jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"timer":"on","instant_feedback":true}']
  resume_state jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{"section_key":"R","position":14,"audio_offset_ms":0}']
  started_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  deadline_at timestamptz [note: 'Server-authoritative end for timed attempts']
  last_activity_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  submitted_at timestamptz
  submit_reason submit_reason
  completed_at timestamptz
  active_seconds integer [not null, default: 0, note: 'Accumulated time on task (excludes paused practice)']

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, started_at) [name: 'ix_attempts_history']
    (user_id, status) [name: 'ix_attempts_resume', note: 'Partial: WHERE status = in_progress']
    (status, deadline_at) [name: 'ix_attempts_deadline_sweep', note: 'Partial: WHERE status = in_progress AND deadline_at IS NOT NULL — auto-submit job']
    exam_revision_id [name: 'ix_attempts_revision']
  }

  checks {
    `mode = 'practice' OR exam_revision_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_attempts_mock_has_revision']
    `(status = 'in_progress') = (submitted_at IS NULL)` [name: 'ck_attempts_submitted_at']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One learner sitting = historical fact. Same engine for practice sets, section tests
and full mocks (TOEIC and IELTS): exam differences live in revision sections/rules and
the scoring policy, not in separate attempt systems. Guest attempts are ordinary attempts
of a guest user. Exam-mode rules are enforced server-side (deadline, review lock).
'''
}

Table attempt_responses {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  attempt_id uuid [not null, ref: > attempts.id]
  question_id uuid [not null, ref: > questions.id, note: 'Exact question version served']
  section_key text [note: 'NULL for adaptive practice']
  position integer [not null]
  max_points numeric(5,2) [not null, note: 'Copied from exam_revision_items.points at start']
  answer jsonb [note: 'NULL = unanswered. {"choice":"B"} | {"text":"..."} | {"pairs":{...}}']
  answer_asset_id uuid [ref: > content_assets.id, note: 'Speaking recording']
  is_flagged boolean [not null, default: false, note: 'Mark for review']
  first_answered_at timestamptz
  last_saved_at timestamptz
  time_spent_ms integer [not null, default: 0]
  is_correct boolean [note: 'Deterministic key grading; NULL for essay/speaking or ungraded']
  points_awarded numeric(5,2) [note: 'Key-graded points, or the current evaluation result']
  graded_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (attempt_id, position) [unique, name: 'uq_attempt_responses_position']
    (attempt_id, question_id) [unique, name: 'uq_attempt_responses_question']
    question_id [name: 'ix_attempt_responses_question', note: 'Item analytics (p-value, distractors)']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One row per SERVED question, created when the attempt starts (unanswered = answer
NULL), so navigation, flags, resume and "unanswered" counts are trivial. Autosave =
UPDATE answer/last_saved_at (last write wins per question). max_points/position are
copied on purpose: the row is the historical record of what was served.
Objective grading writes is_correct/points_awarded here; subjective feedback lives in evaluations.
'''
}

Table evaluations {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  response_id uuid [not null, ref: > attempt_responses.id]
  evaluator_kind evaluator_kind [not null]
  evaluator_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id, note: 'Teacher for human evaluations']
  ai_run_id uuid [ref: > ai_runs.id]
  status evaluation_status [not null, default: 'pending']
  rubric_key text [not null, note: 'Copied from question at evaluation time']
  criteria_scores jsonb [note: '{"task_response":6.5,"coherence":6,"lexical":6.5,"grammar":6}']
  estimated_score numeric(5,2) [note: 'AI/teacher band estimate for this response']
  feedback jsonb [note: '{summary, strengths[], improvements[], inline:[{span, suggestion}]}']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  completed_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (response_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_evaluations_response', note: 'Partial unique (response_id) WHERE status = completed — one current evaluation']
  }

  checks {
    `(evaluator_kind = 'ai') = (ai_run_id IS NOT NULL)` [name: 'ck_evaluations_ai_run']
    `evaluator_kind <> 'human' OR evaluator_user_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_evaluations_human_evaluator']
  }

  Note: '''
[P2] Subjective assessment of Writing/Speaking responses, kept apart from deterministic
key grading. AI evaluations are always labeled "AI estimate"; a teacher evaluation (P4)
supersedes the AI one (status superseded) without deleting it.
'''
}

Table attempt_scores {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  attempt_id uuid [not null, ref: > attempts.id]
  scope text [not null, note: '"overall" or a section_key ("L","R","W","S")']
  score_kind score_kind [not null]
  value numeric(7,2) [not null]
  max_value numeric(7,2) [not null]
  scale text [not null, note: 'points | toeic_section | toeic_total | ielts_band']
  scoring_policy_key text [not null, note: 'Scorer version that produced this value']
  computed_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (attempt_id, scope, score_kind) [unique, name: 'uq_attempt_scores_scope_kind']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Score facts per attempt. Stored (not derived on read) because conversion tables and
AI models change; history must show what the learner saw. Percent = value/max_value
(derived, not stored). There is no "official" score_kind: Engrisk never issues official
scores. Per-skill breakdown is derived from responses + question_skills.
'''
}

Table learner_skill_stats {
  tenant_id uuid [not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  skill_id uuid [not null, ref: > skills.id]
  responses_count integer [not null, default: 0]
  correct_count integer [not null, default: 0]
  mastery numeric(4,3) [note: '0..1 recency-weighted estimate']
  last_practiced_at timestamptz
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, skill_id) [pk]
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] Derived read model for dashboard "weak skills" and recommendations; updated when an
attempt is graded and fully rebuildable from attempt_responses + question_skills.
Exists only for read performance — not a source of truth.
'''
}

// =============================================================================
// 6. AI PROVENANCE & TUTOR
// =============================================================================

Table ai_runs {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null, ref: > tenants.id]
  requested_by_user_id uuid [ref: > users.id]
  purpose ai_purpose [not null]
  status ai_run_status [not null, default: 'queued']
  provider text [not null, note: 'openai | anthropic | google | self_hosted']
  model text [not null]
  model_version text
  prompt_key text [not null, note: 'Prompt template id in code']
  prompt_version text [not null]
  input_refs jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: 'Ids only: {"response_id":..} {"source_material_id":..}']
  usage jsonb [not null, default: `'{}'::jsonb`, note: '{input_tokens, output_tokens, cost_usd, latency_ms}']
  error_code text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  started_at timestamptz
  finished_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, purpose, created_at) [name: 'ix_ai_runs_tenant_purpose']
    (requested_by_user_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_ai_runs_user', note: 'Per-user quota checks']
    (status, created_at) [name: 'ix_ai_runs_queue', note: 'Partial: WHERE status IN (queued, running)']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] One row per AI invocation = provenance + async job state + cost/quota ledger.
Outputs are stored in the domain row that uses them (questions, evaluations,
tutor_messages), which points back here. Raw prompts/completions are NOT stored in
PostgreSQL (privacy); short-retention logs only. No separate generation-job table.
'''
}

Table tutor_conversations {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  tenant_id uuid [not null]
  user_id uuid [not null]
  attempt_id uuid [ref: > attempts.id, note: 'Context: opened from a result']
  response_id uuid [ref: > attempt_responses.id, note: 'Context: "Explain this answer"']
  question_id uuid [ref: > questions.id, note: 'Context when opened outside an attempt']
  title text
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  updated_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]
  archived_at timestamptz

  indexes {
    (tenant_id, user_id, updated_at) [name: 'ix_tutor_conversations_user']
    response_id [name: 'ix_tutor_conversations_response']
  }

  Note: '''
[P1] AI tutor thread, usually anchored to a response so the tutor is grounded on the
verified answer key + explanation. Private to the learner (tenant admins see usage counts,
not content — open question in product_flow.md M).
'''
}

Table tutor_messages {
  id uuid [pk, default: `gen_random_uuid()`]
  conversation_id uuid [not null]
  sender message_sender [not null]
  body text [not null]
  ai_run_id uuid [ref: > ai_runs.id, note: 'Set for tutor messages']
  grounding jsonb [not null, default: `'[]'::jsonb`, note: 'Cited sources: [{"type":"answer_key","question_id":..},{"type":"explanation"}]']
  learner_rating smallint [note: '-1 not helpful, 1 helpful']
  created_at timestamptz [not null, default: `now()`]

  indexes {
    (conversation_id, created_at) [name: 'ix_tutor_messages_conversation']
  }

  checks {
    `sender <> 'tutor' OR ai_run_id IS NOT NULL` [name: 'ck_tutor_messages_ai_provenance']
  }

  Note: '[P1] Messages in a tutor thread. Tutor messages always carry provenance; grounding lets the UI separate "Verified answer key" from "AI explanation".'
}

// =============================================================================
// TENANT-CONSISTENCY & SCOPE COMPOSITE FOREIGN KEYS
// =============================================================================

// Role scope guards
Ref: platform_role_assignments.(role_id, role_scope) > roles.(id, scope)
Ref: membership_roles.(role_id, role_scope) > roles.(id, scope)

// Session tenant context must be a membership of the session user
Ref: auth_sessions.(active_tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)

// Learner data lives inside a membership
Ref: source_materials.(tenant_id, owner_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: learner_goals.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: attempts.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: learner_skill_stats.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: tutor_conversations.(tenant_id, user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)

// Private content owners must be members of the owning tenant
Ref: question_groups.(tenant_id, owner_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: questions.(tenant_id, owner_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)
Ref: exams.(tenant_id, owner_user_id) > tenant_memberships.(tenant_id, user_id)

// Authoring graph stays inside one tenant
Ref: source_materials.(tenant_id, asset_id) > content_assets.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: question_groups.(tenant_id, audio_asset_id) > content_assets.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: question_groups.(tenant_id, image_asset_id) > content_assets.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: question_groups.(tenant_id, source_material_id) > source_materials.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: questions.(tenant_id, question_group_id) > question_groups.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: questions.(tenant_id, source_material_id) > source_materials.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: exam_revisions.(tenant_id, exam_id) > exams.(tenant_id, id)
Ref: exam_revision_items.(tenant_id, exam_revision_id) > exam_revisions.(tenant_id, id) [delete: cascade]
Ref: exam_revision_items.(tenant_id, question_id) > questions.(tenant_id, id)

// Compositions (child rows have no meaning without parent)
Ref: tutor_messages.conversation_id > tutor_conversations.id [delete: cascade]

// =============================================================================
// TABLE GROUPS
// =============================================================================

TableGroup identity_access [color: #3B82F6] {
  users
  auth_identities
  auth_sessions
  auth_tokens
  roles
  permissions
